    "max_to_min_ratio": 12109,
    "why_unified_model": "The most-tested agent has 108,981 rows and the least-tested has 9. 16 of 54 agents have fewer than 1,000 rows and 5 have fewer than 100. A separate model per antibiotic is therefore untrainable for most of the panel, and a multi-label target would be ~76% missing by construction because each isolate is only tested against the agents the laboratory selected. A single unified model with the antibiotic and its class as input features uses every row and lets a rare agent inherit structure from its class \u2014 which is the only way to score an agent the laboratory did not test."
  },
